#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0fcd6c1-3e34-5869-bda3-f3935c249cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in L$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396601} {:answer/id #uuid "9ae69b77-733b-5c58-bc2b-3800bcfe26dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396602} {:answer/id #uuid "dac8d022-edf8-56b5-99c7-7f2b00e051d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions in $L$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396603} {:answer/id #uuid "6358779e-1da8-5238-9ef6-81ac25fc065f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions in $L$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396604} {:answer/id #uuid "85442eb9-7db8-592f-9879-ddfd77d97231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ae69b77-733b-5c58-bc2b-3800bcfe26dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396602} :answer-field/id #uuid "f09dfa2c-f035-539f-94db-4698ecc43f0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15beea94-47dc-575a-be81-e2d3b2547e2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106930" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)=ax+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$L$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **multiplication of $f\\in L$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)=x+1,$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2x+2.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin L$ because the constant term is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in L.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of real valued functions satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96cab4fe-b011-5072-be3e-391125bf75c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399589} {:answer/id #uuid "479eb2f9-8717-57b1-9f07-9c964bbfdbab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399590} {:answer/id #uuid "fcde83fb-02ab-5892-a45a-6c4b43adb9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399591} {:answer/id #uuid "e44c72a4-6813-558a-a34c-560c1aff92da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399592} {:answer/id #uuid "afcd5ca7-6625-5f48-ac5f-5ce7f390cf1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e44c72a4-6813-558a-a34c-560c1aff92da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399592} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb9d1c7-c909-596f-a04a-7d5c7e74340d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "258def85-3c26-5841-81d2-c1a1f3c916a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-106944" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$0\\cdot 0=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A5}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "313cdc82-5d69-5af4-95bb-ace914a012ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418996} {:answer/id #uuid "4f43eb35-6698-556b-937a-7540b2eaa194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions in $A$  is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418997} {:answer/id #uuid "54d7d70f-b06b-5dba-8920-ce4be2335648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions in $A$  is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418999} {:answer/id #uuid "61ff392f-4de3-5c34-9123-789573d772b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419000} {:answer/id #uuid "f187a6fa-78fb-565f-9a52-c1915abb65f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions  in $A$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "313cdc82-5d69-5af4-95bb-ace914a012ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418996} :answer-field/id #uuid "4628fceb-08d9-5ba5-86ad-00d444e18706" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a47334c-0a05-5b9c-b7eb-76cf4c1d5cfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-94792" :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form  $f(x)=a+{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because **multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)={x}^{2},$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2{x}^{2}.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin A$ because the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in A.$ $\\,✓$"}]}
